<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Goto (230)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>goto &lt;room@zone&gt;
goto &lt;zone&gt;
goto &lt;someone or something&gt;
goto &lt;room&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>goto inn@udgaard
goto midgaard
goto Papi
goto corpse
</pre>
<p>The gods' way of travelling: at once, to anywhere in the world. You land 
in the room of what you name, or inside it if it is something one can 
enter, such as a ship. In order, goto tries:
</p>
<ol><li>a symbolic name, room@zone (or any unit@zone: you go to where it is);</li>
<li>a corpse, when the word corpse is in the name;</li>
<li>a zone's name: its first room;</li>
<li>a player, then a room, a monster and a thing, anywhere, by name;</li>
<li>a room of that symbolic name in your own zone.</li></ol>
<p>You can't go into a private room where two players already are. You are 
warned if the place doesn't allow teleporting, but go all the same. The 
room sees you disappear into thin air and appear from thin air (or your 
own $bamfout and $bamfin texts, if your character has those extra 
descriptions), and you look around. It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp At</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Transfer</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Corpses</a>
</pre>




</div>